  "label": "The text 'the first rule of deaf club..' is mapped onto the scene of sign language communication.",
  "description": "The top text 'the first rule of deaf club..' is juxtaposed with the visual of a woman using American Sign Language (ASL) to communicate. This creates an analogical mapping where the text refers to a rule governing the 'deaf club' (the deaf community), and the visual material (the woman signing) represents a member of that club actively engaging in its communication method. The mapping implies that the visual scene is an instance of the 'rule' being enacted or referenced.",
